editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:151:- **Her case, as said on the 268th (flag; the place itself is now given only in her restored protected speech):** mine are the two steps before it: "I think that they are instructions." (the same forty-one kinds in the same order on three floors; a line that carries the circle's own measure), and that a key to the index exists and "is kept". The hide lies on Seln's oilcloth with the brass along its pencil line. Then the coordinator's three joins and the protected speech, in which **"west", "Treswick" and "the Deepstacks" are said aloud for the first time**. My earlier description of the archive, of the provision and of Karis's certificate is gone. **After the speech, mine:** Seln adds only what the speech does not have (a gate with a book in it; a station on its crown; the paper that executes "on the hour when any of us shows a certificate inside the Line"; one file not shut); Lira's certificate ("Iron, Rank One, with a seal on it"); Cael's "A registry's where they file you"; no ruling. The scene closes on "her first two words", which none of the six had ever said aloud as a place to go.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:170:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **She has made her case to six** (the 268th): instructions; an index with a key that is kept; and then, in her protected speech, west, Treswick, the registry office on the old town, the Deepstacks under it, the old scholars' provision for a registered historical-studies practitioner, which she is not, and "a man there who is" (unnamed). She said the sentence whole to Cael on the 263rd, without the word west. She cannot read the four signs and has put no meaning on the stroke and the bar. She knows how the kit's cord is used and has taught the five. She has entered the anomaly as *Cause: not found. No inference entered.* and has written no sentence joining it to anything. Fifty-two sheets; the hide; the kit; the dead man's ledger, open now; a hair in her notebook. She keeps the purse.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:186:**Words said aloud for the first time.** *West* (as the place to go), *Treswick* and *the Deepstacks*: all three by Karis, in her protected speech at the board on the 268th, and by nobody before it. Cael writes *West, and inside* on the 270th. Not said at all: Cleon's name; Vastin's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:205:**Movement 1 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Sol recheck of repair r1: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all four tracked passages RESOLVED against the source; no new tracking; every binding ruling above borne out by the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch3, the author's own "his Path" (of Teague) now reads "the Force"; ch6, Seln's sentence after Karis's protected speech now gives the asset-restriction as locked Book 6 ch58 states it — **the paper executes when an enrolled name is written in a book inside a district, and must be served within the hour** (not "a certificate inside the Line"). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report after the fixes. Final: 30,941 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (9 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment twenty-nine; day 270 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:214:- **What Vastin added about the layer is exactly four things:** it cannot be reached (there is no key); a citation to a designer; the suppressed survey records; the technician's line. The layer's existence was Karis's already (her protected line stands unglossed, OWNER-pending #48). Nothing says that menders, technicians or any office know more; nothing says it has been tried.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:215:- **The three papers.** (1) **The records:** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather; six taped rows, a year to a row, of survey abstracts measured in lengths, knots and strides, with the dead surveyor's four-sign index printed at their heads; an **anomaly column** in which every sheet, in every hand, for six years carries the one word *Total* (an entry, not a sum; no figure); "More than four" (Karis, counting distinct sign-groups; she gives no number); the Fallow completion report is the last, loose sheet, and carries **five strokes for a name and a count of six** (locked Book 7 ch40, ch43), not five names. (2) **The page:** a COPY in Vastin's own hand of one line from an old register, carried in oilcloth in his coat: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". "The Architect" is a title, not a name, and a word Karis has never met in any stratum. It is never called a leaf; **the leaf has not appeared**. (3) **The technician's sheet:** the two protected lines with a date between them, a brush bar across what followed, and Karis's *not read*. **The date is a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it, and is never printed as figures** (the source gives none; no owner decision is needed). The office had filed the sheet at the end of the second row and it lies there again.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:217:- **Speakers (protected):** "Archmarshal" is Cael's; "What follows you," is Lira's; "More than four." is Karis's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," is Oryn's (Karis owns the order to bed). The long table's close is verbatim. "Nothing that can cross the Line"; the rim of the Stair "is not mine".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:226:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (1 tracked passage, ch12 scene 3; probe 2% / 12%, the excess being protected and plan-quoted document text); plan / canon / protected-text audit (REPAIR; 46 exact fixes, of which the coordinator applied 24 — protected units restored, two speakers corrected, "leaf" to "page" — and sent 22 to the author to recompose in voice). Coordinator rulings against the audit: the technician's date is NOT owner-pending (the source prints no value; the page shows a date and no figures); the completion report carries five strokes, not five names (Book 7 ch43:51), where the audit's fix kept "five names". **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:292:**Movement 2 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the 24 coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed; the page made a copy; the layer cut to four facts (Lira and Brom say what it changes: there is nobody to ask); *Total* made the anomaly column's entry; the technician's sheet read out by Lira with a date and no figures, filed at and laid back at the end of the second row; Seln's stillness re-entered in a new order; receipt and night log made literally true ("Read in part. Understood in no part."); the completion report's five strokes and count of six; ch7's opening oriented. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling above borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (ice 111 days; the wrist 124; the sling 170; the rim 163; the cord 109; the report 175). Three fixes applied by the coordinator: ch7 "a healer's Path" → "a healer's craft" (no possessive before Path in narration); ch8's bluff memory cut back to what Book 5 shows; ch10 "through a frame shop" removed. Rulings from the recheck: **Lira reading the sheet aloud is the author's staging and stands** (the map protects the wording, the sum and the withholding, not the reader); the two descriptions of the cited record agree. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 30,105 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (11 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; the night before day 278 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:312:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (3 tracked passages, none dense; probe 2% / 15%); plan / canon / protected-text audit (REPAIR; 102 exact fixes). Coordinator rulings against the audit, after checking the source and the locked Book 7: the cut's staging, the Ember use and the count of thirty-two KEPT (BOOK_MAP §8: private staging the author owns; the audit's 39 re-staging fixes declined); Oryn's past KEPT; Cael's touch of the page KEPT; the slip left as the packet quotes it; "every bar of a fence" KEPT (Book 7 ch58). Accepted from the audit: the six markers' speakers (two filled with the plan's own clause only); the loads for Movement 4; no fifth place or number; no second calendar; the remark's hand unidentified. Eleven fixes applied by the coordinator; the rest recomposed by the author. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:331:- **The abstracts, read in daylight.** Karis counted every row twice and had each counted again; **no figure for any row is printed**. **She gives no number of places.** She sorted the sheets by their sign-groups, matched **four** to the hide by their measures (three alike to the stride, one double), and will not call the unmatched groups places until a sign can be read (17:27–39). **Five columns:** the day, in the registry's reckoning; the station (eight points); the measure; *Instruments*; and the anomaly. No radius of the four has changed by a stride in six years; four surveyors by their figures; three clerks' hands. The fourth column reads *Cord true. Edge true. Level true.* on every sheet. The three oldest rows have a ruled space at the foot headed *Remarks*, empty but once: **the Stair's sheet in the fourth row carries the protected four words, in a hand that is none of the three clerks'; Karis laid the dead man's ledger beside it and will not swear to the hand either way.** From the next year's printing the space is gone. Brom counts the three findings on his fingers (17:61, 17:77, 17:139).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:388:**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (ch13, ch16–19; ch14–15 untouched): the eleven coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Seln on the north bank beside the factor; Cael had not known that he would say "You do now,"; Vastin names the town); no number of places and no fifth place (Karis counted groups, not places; four matched to the hide; the other sheets' corners turned down, uncounted and undescribed); the second calendar cut (Seln knew the day because he had copied that line of Cael's file twice; Cael laid the date he knows against the sheet's, a figure at a time, twice); three tracked passages re-ordered; the ruler line verbatim at the stopped lamps sentence; the remark's hand unidentified; Brom counts the spring's three findings on his fingers; the loads and the closing file made to meet Movement 4 (**Vastin took the kit case against the letter of Oryn's "you're not to" and told Cael so at once; Oryn does not know**; he walks a shoulder off Cael's left from a dozen strides down the rise). Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the settled rulings (the cut's staging, thirty-two, Oryn's past, the hand on the page) confirmed in the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch16 "Two days ago, at a board" (was three); ch18 Seln "has spent fifteen years among the seat's paper" (he copied for twelve). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 34,751 prose words (about 2% over; accepted — the added scene carries the loads and the seam); gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (16 protected). Purse 138 marks; deployment thirty-two; day 281, near noon, going down off the rise toward Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:396:- **The reading inward (the 281st): the fourth and fifth self-readings**, with Tide, ROUND the still place and never in; **not counted** ("Myself, twice: not counted, as before"); a palm on a gatepost while it was open is a trial. Finding (protected): "He had been putting a cord on a stone and writing down *no length*." — the tenth feels only what flows; where nothing flows it returns nothing, and that nothing is the instrument's limit, not a finding about the place (a gatepost and the middle of himself come back alike). **He needs an instrument for what does not move.** He read Oryn's order for the leave he wanted, has logged that, and **owes her the telling at the mill before anything else is said**. Lira asked and is entered as having asked. **Deployment since the Line: thirty-two; ten fragments; none acquired.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:397:- **Vastin and Cael at the three-mile post.** Vastin SAT for the first time since the cut, of his own choosing, where he could not rise without Cael's arm. "I read your file" (no span of years). Cael: "You were the instrument," … "I was the error." (protected, Cael's). **Why he declined** (the author's, amended to locked Book 6): the case shown him at Ostrand is the true and causal reason — the office had shown him what it did with honest readings; and privately part of him was relieved never to learn what a plate would say (a second silence would have been turned on Cael; a plate that lit would have been turned on nine thousand of his own readings). A sound act, and glad of it for a bad reason. **What Cael gave him:** that the place has been read twice that day with "the one thing I've got that reads", and nothing came back because that thing only feels what moves. NOT what reads, nor fragments, the mechanism, the date. Vastin did not ask. "It is a place where two people can stand": ground, not friendship. The S7 log verbatim ("color" stands).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:398:- **Treswick (the 282nd).** The grey bridge on five piers is of dark, dry-laid stone with no mortar and is OLDER than the walls (Karis, from the masons' fitting of the pale stone to it); the same dark stone is the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the frame of the iron door. The outer gate: one keeper counts feet on a bead-frame ("Six"); another writes only loads that come on wheels to be sold. **No name of the six was written.** The outer district works by brokers' slate boards and counted labour: cards with a coloured edge (blue to the second wall, buff to the third) carry a figure, are counted in with a pen and torn at each gate, and are good for the day named. **Iron passes the second wall by right, Bronze the third** — on a certificate that is read out and WRITTEN. The smith's two forges (charcoal; an Ember's held bed for a horse with a blue band): Brom, "They shoe by the tier." (protected). The rope-walk: sixty yards of four-strand priced (no figure printed) and to be bought going out; the Lowmarch debt stands. **The inn with two doors** (the painted door has a book; the yard half-door takes money): the long loft over the stable for a week from the 282nd, the pot at dusk, seven bowls; two marks paid; **purse 136**. Lira hung a blanket over the loft's uphill window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:402:- **The 284th.** Seln is NOT on the count (a clerk might know his face; somebody must watch the door). **Vastin said "Yes" before a mouth was open** and is the fourth hand. Karis is the card's unnamed bearer; **Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands**. Both upper keepers counted ("One, and four") and tore a corner; the way to the yard goes by the load lane under the third wall and a cut of **twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no door or window** — never across the square. **Cael did not set foot on the square or its steps and did not look at the crown; Lira kept the same discipline unasked** and walked between him and each alley's end. **Lira's ladder did not pull** ("It's a hill with a tax on it"); protected: "Four hands," (Lira) / "Four." (Cael) / "Right." (Lira); the S9 log verbatim. Her registry paper stayed in her coat. **The yard clerk (unnamed) asked nothing and wrote *four*.** None of the four restricted names has been written; the asset-restriction is still pending.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:408:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol), with the audit instructed to separate protected text and plan facts from the source's staging: editorial; cold read; source-distance (2 tracked passages, both in ch26; probe 2% / 10%); plan / canon / protected-text audit (bounded line repair; 10 exact fixes; every piece of the author's staging and city mechanics ratified). Nine fixes applied by the coordinator (five markers restored whole with speakers; the full inward-finding sentence; Shadow's ordinal; Cleon's lamp term; the parapet exchange moved); the tenth (the weighting of Vastin's refusal against Book 6) recomposed by the author. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:425:- **Cleon, as seen.** Not tall; grey hair cut short and badly; a coat the colour of dust; round shoulders; square pale hands with the nails pared to the quick; red-rimmed wet eyes, which he keeps shut while he eats; a voice "like a hinge". He looks at a sheet from its foot upward. He eats at the counter's end by the yard door at noon and goes down within the hour. **Cael knows him for Cleon at the counter** (the name said at a spring) and reads it once, written, at the head of the card in Lira's hands on the 283rd; nobody says it aloud. Karis told him at the counter what the floors are (the protected line: fused, grey, no join; three of them; fifty-two sheets), so his questions after it are of method only (rubbed or drawn; what light; which edge north; how far apart). **His terms (mine, one amended by the audit):** not on a counter; all of them, not a choice; they come down to him and he does not come up; his card, written at the counter (the matter; its bearer, one; hands, a figure), good for the next day only, at the second bell; no names given or wanted; not a word of what she thinks they are until he has looked; **one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says, and no other carried light or fire of anybody's** (a light already burning below is not excluded). He pushed her sheet back without touching it. He left by the street door and stopped a full stride beyond it for three breaths. **He never looked toward the yard.** The Path is not shown; only that he rests his eyes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:455:**Cleon.** Named by the narration in chapter 24 (at the counter, and in the tags of the protected exchange) and once in chapter 26; never said aloud by anybody in this movement; Cael has read the name on the card. Rune Path, Bronze, by Seln's report only. He has set terms, written a card, and pulled the iron to. He has taken no notice of Cael. He has been told what the floors are (fused, grey, no join; three; fifty-two sheets) and nothing of what the sheets are thought to mean.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:478:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (a bounded line repair; nothing re-staged): the nine coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (the boulder image made to agree with "*no length*"; Karis looks at three boxes and a case before "Four hands."; the cook-house questions after the restored exchange are of method only; "Four." given to Cael at the parapet); Vastin's refusal recomposed to locked Book 6 (the Ostrand case stated as the cause, twice, and not taken back; beside it "I had kept my hand off a door for a sound reason, and I was thankful of it for a poor one"; entered "on a form which has no line for why"); the two tracked passages in ch26 re-ordered (Lira prices the ladder aloud and shoulders the box before Cael understands; the clerk writes *four* and blots it before he looks at a face, then opens the door, looks at Vastin, opens his mouth and shuts it); Wind's ceiling removed; **Cleon's name comes to Cael at the cook-house counter and is then read on the card — nobody has said it aloud**; second tellings of the name-versus-count idea trimmed. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; both tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (161 days since the last self-reading; four days since the board; 282 days since the first sill; Oryn's gates). One punctuation fix applied by the coordinator (a broken dialogue join in ch21). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,179 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (12 protected). Purse 136 marks; deployment thirty-two; ten fragments; the forenoon of day 284, inside the iron door under Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:488:- **The yard door, the 285th.** The clerk's form had no line for matter that had gone up and come back; he asked one question ("The same?") and was about to send up for the under-registrar. **Vastin gave his old name, rank and office aloud** (protected: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —"); the clerk's pen came up and **wrote nothing of it**. **Seln, posing as a porter on the hatch's bench, answered truthfully** (protected, whole: "He's on the count. Four hands, same as yesterday, entered by the practitioner and answered for by her, and the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was. The researcher's at your counter and she'll want to be told we're through,"). The clerk wrote *The same* and *four*, and has done so each day since. **The cost: a Treswick registry clerk now knows Seln's face and voice.** "I'm sorry." (Vastin) / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." (Seln). Seln watches from the roof above the cut's head from then on. No restricted name has been written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:491:- **Vastin** went toward the lamp four times on the 287th, twice on the 288th, not at all on the 290th. "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:493:- **THE ELEVENTH.** In that quiet minute **Cael acquired Iron-Wall-adjacent, from Vastin** — it did not fill, it *set*, "as a post is stood in its hole"; its prompt is *This far?*; he has told it no each time. **Not deployed. Not told to Vastin.** The protected lines are Cael's own cataloguing, printed once in italics (not a system block): "Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. … Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh." **Eleven fragments; deployment since the Line: thirty-two.** Vastin: "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered…" ("it" is what Cael is, which he could not read) / "It's entered," — and Cael has entered more than the man knows: **a debt he cannot yet pay** ("Not told. I can't tell the taking without telling the rest, and the rest is six people's"). Lira has read the log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:499:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (1 tracked passage, ch27 scene 2; probe 2% / 14%); plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES; ten exact fixes; all nineteen author flags and every minted item KEPT). Eight applied by the coordinator (five markers restored whole with speakers — two of Cleon's had been staged as Karis's — and three joins). Two DECLINED: the audit wanted the eleventh's lines printed as system text under a FRAGMENT ACQUIRED heading; the protected unit is Cael's own cataloguing (it names Vastin and says "Eleventh"; the twelfth says "me"), so the author's frame stands and the coordinator set the unit in italics instead of a code fence. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:515:- **Cleon's week (as repaired).** On the 284th, from his chair, with his eyes shut, Cleon said what being believed was to him (protected) and then asked for a week (protected: "Give me a week."); Karis asked the five for the same week in her own words ("I should like his week"), and Cael said that it was hers. On the 287th he re-set it: he had spent the half of the first on his own page, which he read every morning before he would look at hers; that is put by, and the week is his, from that day, with nothing else on the desk. At its end every sheet goes up and the clerk writes that it is gone (he will not have matter lying a month under *the same*). Its seventh day is the 293rd; three days are left after the 290th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:569:- **Inn, purse, count and day.** Six are in the long loft over the stable; it is paid through the 295th, with pot at dusk and seven bowls. Purse 134, reserve sealed in the third box. The below-ground daily count remains Karis as bearer plus four hands; Seln is never one of them. Night of day 290 is complete; Movement 6 opens day 291. The cut will not be climbed at dusk again, but no further route ruling has been made (`chapter-31.md:265–267`; `chapter-33.md:277–305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:101–103,123`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:573:**Movement 5 CLOSED (2026-10-12).** Same-author repair r1 (ch27–31; ch32–33 untouched apart from the eleventh's lines set in italics): the eight coordinator-applied fixes kept and re-joined — **ch27's scene at the Hall's table now turns on Cleon** (Cael's "Then what is it?" goes to Karis, who does not answer; Cleon, eyes shut at his desk, says the "Being believed" unit to himself in the hearing of five; Karis tells Brom who has believed him; Cleon opens his eyes for "Give me a week."; **Karis then asks the five in her own words — "I should like his week" — and Cael says it is hers**); ch30, Cleon re-sets his own week from the 287th (half the first went on his own page each morning; that is put by); ch31's opening keeps only her side of being believed; Seln's line at the hatch whole, with the narration noting that he said nothing that was not in the clerk's own book or at his ledge, "and he had said *we*, which lay in no book at all"; Cleon's close whole with the author's joins. The tracked passage re-ordered (Cleon gives his table orders over his shoulder with his finger on his line; when Cael looks again the chair is empty and the leaf lies face up, unmarked); two physical anchors in the cipher proof; restated method compressed; first-use anchors added. Sol recheck: **CLOSE, no line fixes**; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the coordinator's ruling on the eleventh's lines (Cael's own cataloguing, in italics, not a system block) treated as settled and consistent on the page. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,987 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (17 protected). Purse 134 marks; deployment thirty-two; **eleven fragments**; the night of day 290, in the loft at Treswick.
