   436	## 12. Canon conflicts found in the source (with the edition's working ruling)
   437	
   438	- **C1 — Vastin's age.** No numeric age for Vastin appears in plan, packet, narration or dialogue; "forty years" is career length only. OWNER #8/#17 govern. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11] OWNER-DECISIONS #8/#17 default: *age never stated; career "forty years"*. **Edition: no stated age.** "Forty years" is kept as his own rounding (ruling 20). *Owner ruling welcome; it does not block.*
   439	- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** no numeric span since Kindling. Anchor academy/cache spans to events; office survey records may keep their own six-year rounding where explicitly identified as the office's. The protected S8 four-year line remains word for word under [OWNER-pending #53] and is never repeated as fact. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
   440	- **C3 — Oryn's days past her road.** S20 has "two days past the end of the road that had been hers" (305th) and S23 "three days past" (307th). The cairn where her road turns north is on the 300th, which makes them five and seven days. **Edition: count from the cairn**, or drop the number.
   441	- **C4 — The grandmother.** The universe ledger lists "Hesk's grandmother" as the owner of the straightedge saying. Book 7 edition chapter 60's note (chapter-60.md:67) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11] ("Your grandmother said…") and S17/S24 make her **Cael's** grandmother, Hesk's late wife. **Edition follows the prose.** The ledger line is a slip.
   442	- **C5 — Rune's tier.** The universe bible says "Cael's twelfth (Rune-adjacent, partial, Bronze)". The notice says "Rune family … Tier equivalent unknown". **Edition follows the notice.** Bronze is Cleon's tier.
   443	- **C6 — Architecture residue.** The architecture's header, plant ledger and checkpoint still say Cael turns twenty in Ch14, the terminus is "the Still Court", and there is a "sixth" site. **Superseded** by rulings 12 and 13 and by the closed prose: nineteen throughout, "the court", the fifth.
   444	- **C7 — Reveal locus.** CANON_RULES says "ancient records in edge-territory ruins"; the bible says a "pre-Compact archive at a border city". The source stages both: the leaf is in the Treswick archive and its key is the ruins' carvings. **Flag for the bible pass.**
   445	- **C8 — Fragment trajectory.** The bible's "22 integrations by Book 10" leaves nine for Book 9 and the Book 10 skip. DECISIONS row 11 left this OPEN with a proposal (≈17 by Book 10, 22 by Book 11). **Not Book 8's to settle.** Book 9's planner must plan the rate and say so.
   446	- **C9 — Lira's paper.** S8 calls it Lira's paper "on paper from a circuit". Canon (Book 5) makes her Iron R1 **formal at the Ostrand station**. **Edition:** "her registry paper", Iron, first rank, formal, carried unshown.
   447	- **C10 — The "first entry inside walls".** S14 calls the 292nd inventory "the first entry in the plain hand that had ever been made in a city", but daily log entries are written inside Treswick on the 282nd, 285th and 290th. **Edition:** it is the first *inventory* (the year's ledger form) written inside walls.
   448	- **C11 — "Tell Lira's family I said so"** (S24 letter to Hesk, kept by the final review). The referent is unclear: no Book 8 scene sets up Hesk carrying word to Lira's family. **Kept verbatim as source-fixed; owner to confirm intent** (it may be a callback the edition's earlier books should plant). [OWNER-pending #55]
   449	- **C12 — Office "six years" and the Kindling date.** "Six years" is the office's survey-record rounding. It is not paired with a numeric count since Cael's Kindling. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
   450	- **C13 — Reader Standard repairs already made in the source.** Seln does not lie at the yard door (ruling 25). Consent is asked before every reading (S18 montage and Cael, S22, S24). **The edition carries both and adds no exception.** The source has no profanity and no gore to remove.
   451	- **C14 — Calendar of the leg.** STATE_RUNNING's first Ch19 note put the cairn on the 301st; the closed prose puts it on the 300th, with the crest on the 303rd. **Edition follows the prose** (§6).
   452	- **C15 — Rhythm (not canon).** The source runs a 21.3-word sentence mean, 19% of sentences at forty words or more, and a paragraph median of 51. The edition re-builds the sentences (§7.4), and Tier C wording stays verbatim.
