   457	
   458	New cold-term, Treswick and leg episodes [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] must leave each of these intact:
   459	- **Lira asks nobody for anything** from Norhold until "Will you mend it." (266th).
   460	- **Cael lies still for no one but Oryn,** and she has read him three times (sack, table, marsh's edge) until Millrace. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling — in the edition's Book 7 Oryn's hands were on Cael for several surface reads that found nothing (the mountain; the ford at Oxhollow; the stake), for the long reading on the 100th (the table), and at the Hall on the 120th (the marsh's edge); Cael has read Oryn twice, each time after asking and an explicit yes.] **Oryn does not read Cael** before Millrace's deep reading; she reads his ribs' surface at most.
   461	- **Seln teaches nobody anything** before "Draft nothing. Just look." (280th, to Vastin).
   462	- **Seln and Vastin exchange no words** before the 277th long-table doorway.
   463	- **No Iron Wall is shown** before the cut (279th). No Force is shown in Cael's presence before the meadow cart (298th).
   464	- **Teague's crew never drills under Vastin's wall** before the pass morning, when the doctrine is told to them once.
   465	- **The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] says nothing to any of the six** until her question at the pass. **The broad man says nothing to them** until "Aye" (305th). **The older healer never speaks to them.** **The young one's name is never written** (said once, by the broad man, in the stream-bed). [OWNER-pending #54]
