     1	# Chapter 16 — What It Was For
     2	
     3	He told Lira on the stair.
     4	
     5	Not the thing. The thing was on a leaf under a registry and in a notebook under Karis's arm, and it had been said once, aloud, in a hole, and was not going to be said again by anyone who had heard it, because a woman had asked that it be the record's and not theirs and the five of them had agreed to that without a word. He told Lira the only thing that was his to tell, which was that the thing she had heard read was on a page now, in Karis's hand, and that she should read the page before anybody talked at her about it, and she said, "Now?" and he said, "At the fire," and she went up the rest of the stair ahead of him with her two hands at her sides and did not look back, because Lira did not look back at a thing she was going to have to look at properly later.
